<!--Post: 9462--><!--Time: 1109535722-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9462"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 12:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Please forgive me, but you may see as this post progresses that it&#39;s not as egotistical as the title would suggest. <BR> <BR>I did a profile of BTK that I published in my <a href="http://www.planethuff.com/darkside/archives/true_crime_serials_btk/index.html#000433">&#34;Dark Side&#34; blog</a> in Dec. of 2004. For corroboration, you can also find a re-post I did in a <a href="http://groups-beta.google.com/group/BTK-Murders/msg/182b2db9a50c768d">little-used Google group.</a> To my knowledge, one cannot edit a Usenet post once it&#39;s up. Just coverin&#39; the bases. <BR> <BR>So, what did I hit, and what did I miss? <i>&#40;And I honestly encourage everyone who did something similar to follow suit. It&#39;s honest and enlightening.&#41;</i> <BR> <BR>Below I&#39;ve posted what I originally wrote. In bold are the things that, based on what I&#39;ve just read today about Denny the Deadly Dog Catcher®, I seem to have nailed. Italics are my duds, my bombs. This can&#39;t be complete because we just don&#39;t know everything yet - but I was beginning to get creeped out, so I figured I&#39;d go ahead. I&#39;ll update with later posts if this thread gets much response. I&#39;ve re-formatted the list of stuff below for this post and added new comments in italicized parentheses on my stupid self. <BR> <BR>================================================== ========================================= <BR> <BR>What follows is, for lack of a better word, a profile. <i>It is most likely completely and utterly wrong.</i> But if it isn&#39;t, you damn sure better come back here and give me my props if they find the dude. I haven&#39;t organized these bullet points, they are written down here as they occur to me - no particular order: <BR> <BR>    &#42; <b>BTK is younger than the age given in the most recently-released info about him. Possibly by a decade or so.</b> <i>&#40;almost-bingo. He was 5 years younger.&#41;</i> <BR> <BR>    &#42; <i>He&#39;s single, and may have been most of his life.</i> &#40;<u>Just dead wrong</u>.&#41; <BR> <BR>    &#42; <b>Resembles the &#39;dark-haired&#39; suspect drawing of him&#40;...&#41;but is not hispanic or italian - he may be balding at this point, but if the mustache was accurate in the drawing, he will still be wearing one. If he&#39;s balding he probably wore a <u>combover</u> <i>&#40;hey, dead-on there. Combovers is evil, yo&#41;</i> until it got too thin,</b> but I suspect his hair will still seem a bit longer than is fashionable for a man his age - no ponytail or anything, but definitely not clippered close to the scalp. <i>&#40;sort of, there.&#41;</i> I know that might disappoint those of you who like the image of some skinhead-looking serial out there with beady eyes in the dark. <BR> <BR>    &#42; <i>I think he no longer kills - the murders may have been inextricably woven into the very fabric of his sexuality, and some factor&#40;s&#41; in his life have weakened the drives that compelled him to murder.</i> I do think that while he no longer kills, he is still perfectly capable of doing so out of self-preservation, or even just for kicks if an opportunity presents itself. The thing is, any murders he may have committed in the last 5 years or so will not seem to be sexual in nature. <i>&#40;basically missed that one, but at this point I&#39;m just guessing. If Hedge and Davis were the only others, I was close here.&#41;</i> <BR> <BR>    &#42; May have been a Mama&#39;s boy. <b>He has a cleanliness fetish, maybe to the point of ocd</b> <i>&#40;read <a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/11004728.htm">this article in the Eagle</a>, the quotes from one Cindy Plant&#41;</i> - it is tied somehow to his upbringing. <BR> <BR>    &#42; Is definitely into trains like the recent profile suggests. I suspect that if he were a ham operator in the 50&#39;s - &#40;actually the sixties, if he is younger as I surmised.&#41; he dropped the hobby. But he will likely own model railroads, and if he&#39;s utilized the internet at all, he&#39;s been doing it for years, and in connection with his railroading hobby, beginning back when there were only message boards for various groups - &#40;alt.comedy, alt.drugs...pick a search term sometime in google and click &#34;groups&#34; instead of &#34;web&#34;. Results can go back into the 80&#39;s.&#41;<i>&#40;I did get Usenet hits for messages from a Dennis Rader, but there&#39;s no way to know if it was him yet, and they weren&#39;t train-related. I <u>think</u> I missed this one.&#41;</i> <BR> <BR>    &#42; <i>I think that in the last year and a half a number of life changes have hammered away at him. Personal, maybe physical - weight gain, diabetes, heart problems - financial. He could have started a business that failed, a loved one could have died. These stresses were the major factors in his re-emergence.</i> Life changes of a certain kind can put one into such a state of anxiety, so undermine one&#39;s confidence that one will act out in ways that are difficult to control, seeking attention, affirmation. With BTK it&#39;s a sort of power being actively sought again, the kind I guess only a serial killer who still presents a dark and foreboding mystery to the people of Wichita, Kansas, or any major city, might enjoy. <BR> <BR>    &#42; <i>I don&#39;t think he has children, but may appear to like them.</i> While I don&#39;t think he&#39;s a pedophile, in spite of his apparent extra focus on one of the two children he killed, &#40;he killed 6 adults we know about, 2 children&#41;, his primary inclination has been toward adult women. I don&#39;t think, by the way, that the race of his victims was significant; I think their personalities and social lives were, though. <BR> <BR>    &#42; <i>He may use his railroading hobby still to ingratiate himself with children. If he has nieces and nephews they may view him as a benign and possibly even sweet old uncle. The railroading hobby may be a big part of his cover, and has been for years - people will view it as unthreatening, even eccentric and charming.</i><u>WRONG</u>. <BR> <BR>    &#42; I believe he will openly tell others photography is a hobby, and if it is, he has his photos extremely well-organized, possibly even labelled and dated. His albums containing photographs of his crimes, taken before he left the scene, will be organized exactly the same as his &#39;normal&#39; albums, but may be in either a safe-deposit box or extremely well-hidden in his home. <i>&#40;Don&#39;t know about a lot of this one yet, but it does look like he hid his trophies at home, and fairly well.&#41;</i> <BR> <BR>    &#42; <b>Co-workers and family alike will have viewed him as helpful, cooperative, the kind of guy who always pitches in. They do not know that his motivation is not altruistic, but aimed at ingratiating himself. Publicly, he wears a mask</b>, and I think he views himself this way too. He viewed BTK&#39;s crimes as his &#34;taking off the mask&#34;, but not in a negative sense, in his mind. More like his unveiling of some great secret. It&#39;s the closest he gets to being mystic. <i>&#40;I get the feeling the first part of this bullet point is spot-on, but his NEIGHBORS in Park City hated him. Church folk loved him.&#41;</i> <BR> <BR>    &#42; A &#34;professional&#34; profile I read said he would be a very lonely individual, seemingly melancholy. I agree with this, but amend it to say that he most likely goes through melancholy &#39;phases&#39;. His family and co-workers may even say to themselves, &#39;oh, he&#39;s in one of his moods.&#39; <i>&#40;not sure on this one yet, but he appears to have been known to be moody, and many neighbors said he was just weird.&#41;</i> <BR> <BR>    &#42; A very, very few who know him well may have seen his temper, as he will have lost it on at least a few occasions. This might be a memory for those friends and family that sticks because it may have seemed very out of character, and perhaps even frightening. I&#39;d bet it also came about as a result of something that seemed trivial to others. <i>&#40;I&#39;m not bolding this point yet, but it appears that Denny got real bent about little stuff...measuring people&#39;s grass with a RULER??&#41;</i> <BR> <BR>    &#42; <i>I also believe the recent info about him moving back in with his Mom in Wichita after a stint in the military. I think this wasn&#39;t a big deal to him, and he may have simply stayed with his mom all the way up to her death. He may be living in her old house right now, or did at least for a time after her passing. If he&#39;s moved, he&#39;s moved to be near family, perhaps even moved in with them. This factor would be one of the things restricting his behavior, keeping him from communicating with police and press more often.</i> <u>Essentially wrong there, Steve-o.</u> <BR> <BR>    &#42; Those around him might have noticed an obvious change in his behavior after the arrest on December 2. I do not think he is a very talkative man, but those around him would have noticed an increased volubility, maybe a spring in his step. One article I read in literature about psychopaths calls this euphoria on the part of con men and killers alike a &#39;duping high.&#39; A charge the subject gets from pulling a con, from evading capture, from getting away with murder. <i>&#40;Don&#39;t know yet on this one.&#41;</i> <BR> <BR>    &#42; <b>Couple of odd thoughts to end this with; I think he still attends church. I think he helps out at church, probably just went to an advent service or a hanging of the greens in the last week or two</b> <i>&#40;wrote this in December, remember...&#41;</i>. I have a very strong feeling he spotted, or even became acquainted with at least one of his victims through some mutual church affiliation. The last thought is about his clothing. The same profile that postulated BTK seeming melancholy, if I recall correctly, also posed the idea that he tends to wear dark clothing by choice. <b>I agree with that, and I also say he keeps his clothes very neat, may be a compulsive ironer - irons his socks and t-shirts too. I say too that he will wear large dark framed glasses, and if they are metal framed they will still be large</b> <i>&#40;ibid on the article linked in the Eagle above, y&#39;all. I smacked this one outta the park, if I say so mah damn self&#41;</i>, and possibly tinted. <i>&#40;In one of his photos and the video at KSN of Denny, it does appear he&#39;s wearing prescription tinted specs, but I&#39;m not sure enough on this to brag about it.&#41;</i> <BR> <BR>================================================== ======================================= <BR> <BR>I do not know why I was clear on his appearance, but I was. I had a POI who shall forever remain unnamed, whom I was obviously wrong about, but a relatively recent photo of my POI closely resembled the majority of the photos I&#39;ve seen of Dennis Rader. I mean, VERY closely - similar build, same large wire-frame glasses, same hairline, almost the same age. <BR> <BR>I was always clear on his ancestry, too - someone at the Eagle forum had long ago posted the assertion that BTK would be of German extraction, and I totally agreed. Rader&#39;s a pretty germanic-sounding name. <BR> <BR>I thought of some other things that seem to be on the mark, put them in various entries at the blog... <BR> <BR>I always thought he was Air Force. He was. I wrote, again in December, the following: <BR> <BR>&#34;<b>...Down south maybe, to the Wichita most folks don&#39;t think of first, Wichita Falls in Texas, where the Air Force has it&#39;s premiere tech school?</b>&#34; <BR> <BR>I considered Navy, but I kept coming back to Air Force. The Tech School connection, the Wichita connection, as tenuous as that seems. <BR> <BR>So that&#39;s it, for now...no work of genius. I know there&#39;s an <u>amateur</u> profile out there somewhere that nailed it, or came mighty close. Love to see it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
